If a patient receives at least 2 overlapping-prescribed-opioids from at least 2 clinicians and the clinicians do not coordinate a care for the patient then every clinician should discuss an increased-respiratory-depression-risk with the patient and should discuss an increased-overdose-risk with the patient and should offer a naloxone-dose to the patient.
If a patient receives an opioid-combination-risk-increasing-medication then every clinician should discuss an increased-respiratory-depression-risk with the patient and should discuss an increased-overdose-risk with the patient and should offer a naloxone-dose to the patient.
